      "dc:description": "In the Pilbara region of Western Australia, the ore reserves occur in a number of widely separated and relatively small deposits, requiring deep mining below the water table, and below sea level at the Goldsworthy pit. The problems discussed are: development of the dewatering system for the Goldsworthy mine, the stability of pit slopes at the Goldsworthy and Shay Gap mines and development of diesel electric trucks for long uphill hauls.",
