      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Mar-Apr",
      "dc:description": "The prevention of erosion from slopes, banks, and batters following open cut mining is an area in which chemicals are being successfully used to achieve the desired results. Most of these products can be classified under one of the following three broad categories: Natural fibrous agents, such as straw, hay, wood shavings, burlap, cloth, tires, and wood mats; synthetic and polymeric materials, such as latex and epoxy compounds, crosslinked polymers, linear polymers crosslinked in place, drying oils, and bitumen; rocks and silicates, such as gravel, rip rap and sodium silicates.",
