      "prism:coverDate": "1975-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "1975",
      "dc:description": "In a number of papers, the authors describe what measures are being taken in the German Democratic Republic to protect the environment against the consequences of lignite mining. Special reference is made to the problems of water pollution. In the production process of the lignite works open cut mining is specifically efficient as landscape changing by reduction of areas, devastation and recultivation. It is pointed out that good results were obtained with landscape planning and cultivation by utilization, protection and reproduction of the soil fund and by joint measures in the territory.",
