      "dc:title": "RECENT DEVELOPMENTS IN OPEN CUT MINING AND MACHINES.",
      "dc:creator": "Waldbieser W.",
      "prism:publicationName": "Min Eng Ny",
      "prism:volume": "26",
      "prism:issueIdentifier": "10",
      "prism:pageRange": "43-45",
      "prism:coverDate": "1974-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Oct",
      "dc:description": "While domestic coal production increased only 5% in the past four years, AMAX Coal's production went up 48% in the same period - thanks to a sustained effort in technological innovation. Among innovations, described in the paper, are a Marion Power Shovel Co. # 8950 walking dragline operating at the Ayrshire mine of Evansville, Ind. This rig equipped with a 150-cu yd bucket, will dig a pit to a depth of 160 ft and move 36-million yd/yr of material. Coal is transported from pit to preparation plant by 180-ton capacity Unit Rig trailers, equipped with 1200-hp diesel engines that power electric-wheel motors. The new developments at Leahy mine in Illinois and Belle Ayr mine in Wyoming are also described.",
